{#
   The League System (#leagues). Every figure comes from WorldOverviewService
   rather than from copy — this section once claimed a flat "22 clubs" for all
   eight tiers, which is why no number is written down here.

   ONE LADDER, NOT A TABLE PLUS A PYRAMID. The section used to show the payment
   table and, under it, a list of tier bars that got NARROWER towards the bottom:
   an upside-down pyramid that repeated the tier column of the table above it.
   Each row now carries both: a bar that widens from the elite tier down to the
   player's starting tier (a real pyramid silhouette when the rows stack), then
   that tier's club count and payouts. Below 640px each row folds into the bar
   over a labelled figure strip, so the money never needs a horizontal scroll.

   Club counts: the deepest tier holds one fewer NPC club than the tier above
   because that place is reserved for the player's own club, which is added on
   the device (see LeagueSizeResolver / app:economy:wage-table check 9). It is
   shown as "N + you" so the count reads as a full division, not a missing club.

   The pyramid is the primary country's (world.tiers); the headline total and the
   footer cover every live country, so the footer says which pyramid is drawn.

   Tiers with no value configured print a dash rather than £0, which would read
   as a deliberate figure.
#}
{% set country_names = world.countries|map(c => c.name) %}
{% set tiers = world.tiers %}
{% set tier_total = tiers|length %}

<section class="leagues-section" id="leagues" aria-labelledby="lg-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="leagues-head">
            <div class="leagues-intro">
                <div class="section-label">The League System</div>
                <h2 class="section-title" id="lg-title">{{ world.totals.tierCount }} TIERS. {{ world.totals.npcClubs|number_format }} CLUBS. ONE ASCENT.</h2>
                <p class="section-sub">Start in non-league obscurity at the bottom of the pyramid, playing everyone home and away. Rival clubs have fully simulated squads, staff, finances and tactics, so beating them means building something real. Track live match updates on the 2D matchday pitch at 1x, 2x or 4x speed, or skip straight to the result.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="leagues-scene">
                <div class="scene" data-scene="match">
                    <img alt="Home and away kits above three pixel players" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {% if tiers is not empty %}
            <div class="ladder">
                <table class="ladder-table">
                    <caption class="pixel">THE PYRAMID &amp; WHAT EACH TIER PAYS</caption>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col" class="ladder-th-tier">Division</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Clubs</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Prize money</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">TV deal</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Position pot</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        {% for tier in tiers %}
                            {# 0 at the top tier, 1 at the bottom: drives width and colour. #}
                            {% set depth = tier_total > 1 ? (loop.index0 / (tier_total - 1)) : 1 %}
                            <tr class="ladder-row{% if loop.first %} is-top{% endif %}{% if loop.last %} is-start{% endif %}"
                                style="--depth: {{ depth|round(3) }}">
                                <th scope="row" class="ladder-tier">
                                    <span class="ladder-bar{% if depth < 0.6 %} is-bright{% endif %}">
                                        <span class="ladder-num">T{{ tier.tier }}</span>
                                        <span class="ladder-name">{{ tier.name }}</span>
                                        {% if loop.last and tier_total > 1 %}<span class="ladder-start">&lt; Your start</span>{% endif %}
                                    </span>
                                    {% if loop.first and tier_total > 1 %}<span class="ladder-tag">Elite &gt;</span>{% endif %}
                                </th>
                                <td class="num ladder-clubs" data-label="Clubs">
                                    {%- if loop.last and tier_total > 1 -%}
                                        <span>{{ tier.clubs }} <span class="ladder-you">+ you</span></span>
                                    {%- else -%}
                                        {{ tier.clubs }}
                                    {%- endif -%}
                                </td>
                                <td class="num" data-label="Prize">{{ tier.prizeMoney is null ? '—' : '£' ~ tier.prizeMoney|number_format }}</td>
                                <td class="num" data-label="TV deal">{{ tier.tvDeal is null ? '—' : '£' ~ tier.tvDeal|number_format }}</td>
                                <td class="num" data-label="Pos. pot">{{ tier.leaguePositionPot is null ? '—' : '£' ~ tier.leaguePositionPot|number_format }}</td>
                            </tr>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p class="ladder-note">
                    Season-end payouts{% if country_names is not empty %} in the {{ country_names|first }} pyramid{% endif %}. Climb a tier and the money changes shape entirely.
                </p>
                <p class="ladder-foot">
                    {{ world.totals.npcClubs|number_format }} NPC clubs across {{ country_names|join(', ') }}{% if world.totals.playableCountries == 1 %} only{% endif %} · more countries coming
                </p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</section>
